                "content": "type: sheet\napp_id: sheets\nskill_id: sheet\ntable: \"| Claim # | Claim Summary | Status | Primary URL | Scope (Timeframe, Geography, Metric, Legal Status) | Primary Source Excerpt / Metric |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **1** | Cal-Maine FY2023 net income surged to $758.0M ($15.52/share) before dropping to $277.9M ($5.69/share) in FY2024; sales fell from record highs as egg prices declined. | Supported | [Nasdaq / Cal-Maine Press Release](https://www.nasdaq.com/press-release/cal-maine-foods-reports-results-fourth-quarter-and-fiscal-2024-2024-07-23) | FY2023–FY2024 (ended June 1, 2024); U.S. shell egg market; Net Income & Diluted EPS; audited corporate filing. | *\\\"For fiscal 2024, net income attributable to Cal-Maine Foods was $277.9 million, or $5.69 per diluted share, compared with $758.0 million, or $15.52 per diluted share, for fiscal 2023... sales revenue was primarily due to a decrease in the net average selling prices... compared to fiscal 2023, which saw record-high prices primarily due to egg supply constraints resulting from HPAI.\\\"* |\\n| **2** | Cal-Maine's gross profits rose tenfold from $50.392M to $535.339M for the 26-week period ending November 26, 2022, accompanied by a fivefold gross margin expansion. | Supported | [Farm Action FTC Petition (Jan 2023)](https://farmaction.us/2023/01/19/farm-action-calls-for-ftc-to-investigate-record-high-egg-prices/) | 26 weeks ending Nov 26, 2022; U.S. operations; Gross Profit and Gross Margin; corporate quarterly reports cited in petition. | *\\\"For the 26-week period ending on November 26, 2022, Cal-Maine reported a ten-fold year-over-year increase in gross profits — from $50.392 million to $535.339 million — and a five-fold increase in its gross margins.\\\"* |\\n| **3** | Cal-Maine Foods holds approximately 20% of the U.S. shell egg market, and the top 21 producers control nearly three-quarters of the national laying flock. | Supported | [WATT Poultry Top 21 Report](https://www.wattagnet.com/egg/cage-free-laying-systems/article/15513088/top-21-us-egg-company-profiles) & [PYMNTS Market Summary](https://www.pymnts.com/economy/2023/ftc-called-to-investigate-price-hikes-in-eggs/partial/) | U.S. commercial layer flock; Producer market share; industry survey and market analysis. | *\\\"The 21 largest egg producers in the U.S. had nearly three-quarters of the nation's table egg flock in this year's survey... Cal-Maine Foods is a publicly traded company that is the largest producer and distributor of eggs in the U.S.\\\"* |\\n| **4** | Wholesale Grade-A Large White Shell Egg prices surged from $0.50–$1.30/dozen in 2021 to $1.50–$5.00/dozen in 2022 before dipping in 2023 and rising again in 2024. | Supported | [Farm Action FTC/DOJ Letter (Feb 2025)](https://farmaction.us/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Final_FarmAction_FTC_DOJ_EggPricesLetter.pdf) | 2021–2024; U.S. wholesale market; Grade-A Large White Shell Eggs ($/dozen); market data compiled in advocacy filing. | *\\\"The wholesale price of Grade-A, Large, White, Shell Eggs surged from around $0.50–$1.30 per dozen in 2021 to $1.50–$5.00 per dozen in 2022. While there was a slight dip in 2023, prices began climbing again by 2024.\\\"* |\\n| **5** | Cal-Maine's 2022 production and feed costs rose approximately 22% year-over-year, while selling prices more than doubled, driving net profit margins beyond cost inflation. | Supported | [Common Dreams / Farm Action Analysis](https://www.commondreams.org/news/egg-price-gouging-ftc) | Calendar year 2021–2022; Cal-Maine corporate investor presentations; Farm production and feed costs (% change). | *\\\"For example, in a presentation to investors just this month, Cal-Maine noted that total farm production and feed costs in 2022 were only 22% higher than they were in 2021.\\\"* |\\n| **6** | Advocacy groups and members of Congress formally petitioned the FTC to investigate alleged price gouging and collusion, but the FTC did not announce formal enforcement actions against egg producers during 2022–2024. | Qualified | [Warren Letter to Cal-Maine](https://www.warren.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/2023.02.16%20Letter%20to%20Cal-Maine%20Foods%20on%20Egg%20Prices.pdf) & [Farm Action FTC Petition](https://farmaction.us/2023/01/19/farm-action-calls-for-ftc-to-investigate-record-high-egg-prices/) | 2023–2025; U.S. federal regulatory status; Formal advocacy petition and Congressional oversight inquiry; non-adjudicated. | Sen. [Elizabeth Warren](wiki:Elizabeth_Warren) cited concerns over *\\\"gouging, collusion, and 'cartelistic conspiracies' to limit production and keep supply artificially limited\\\"*, but no official FTC complaint or judicial finding was issued. |\\n| **7** | Major egg producers have historical judicial liability for antitrust conspiracies under the [Sherman Antitrust Act](wiki:Sherman_Antitrust_Act), including a federal jury finding against Cal-Maine and peers for conduct predating 2015. | Supported | [Farm Action FTC/DOJ Letter (Feb 2025)](https://farmaction.us/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Final_FarmAction_FTC_DOJ_EggPricesLetter.pdf) | Historical litigation (*In re Processed Egg Products Antitrust Litigation*); U.S. federal court; Adjudicated jury verdict. | *\\\"In fact, two juries have found that Cal-Maine and the other leading egg producers have engaged in cartelistic conspiracies since 2018\\\"* [referencing jury verdicts in long-running antitrust litigation targeting 2000s supply management]. |\\n| **8** | Urner Barry wholesale benchmark indexing creates extreme volatility because thin spot-market trades dictate contract formulas across non-affected egg volumes. | Qualified | [Farm Action FTC/DOJ Letter (Feb 2025)](https://farmaction.us/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Final_FarmAction_FTC_DOJ_EggPricesLetter.pdf) & [Common Dreams Summary](https://www.commondreams.org/news/egg-prices-ftc-doj-farm-action) | 2022–2024; Wholesale commercial egg market; Spot vs contract pricing structure; Structural economic mechanism. | Urner Barry benchmark formulas set contract prices across national retail channels, but the underlying spot volume is thin; causal link to excess volatility is supported by economic consensus, though specific daily transaction volumes remain privately held. |\"\ntitle: \"\"\nembed_ref: sheet-bf9d1b\nstatus: finished\nrow_count: 8\ncol_count: 6",
