                "content": "type: search_result\ntitle: Farm Action Calls for FTC to Investigate Record-High Egg Prices | Farm Action\nurl: \"https://farmaction.us/2023/01/19/farm-action-calls-for-ftc-to-investigate-record-high-egg-prices/\"\ndescription: \"Farm Action’s letter lays out the economic basis for its “concerns over apparent price gouging, price coordination, and other unfair or deceptive acts or practices by dominant producers of eggs,” including market giant and industry ...\"\nage: \"February 13, 2025\"\npage_age: \"February 13, 2025\"\nlanguage: en\nfamily_friendly: true\nprofile_name: Farm Action\nmeta_url_favicon: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/i2kgXu7jbLgweiJrFFLNsH31gqqMw8v5DSMy1C9MQao/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMWM1YTY3ZGFi/MjM5YWI2MzIyZWE1/NjMwMmZlZGQyMzcz/NzViZjI0ODg4ZGQ0/MWM3NWMxMTdmM2Mx/ZjUxYzk4ZC9mYXJt/YWN0aW9uLnVzLw\"\nthumbnail_src: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/N2w1DRdxoUElokTPRD42yqqaMzwTyK8x_SAGEy7j6Mg/rs:fit:200:200:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cHM6Ly9mYXJt/YWN0aW9uLnVzL3dw/LWNvbnRlbnQvdXBs/b2Fkcy8yMDIzLzAx/L0NvbXByZXNzZWRf/QWRvYmVTdG9ja18z/MTMyNzg3NDIuanBn\"\nthumbnail_original: \"https://farmaction.us/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/Compressed_AdobeStock_313278742.jpg\"\nextra_snippets: \"On the heels of this letter, Farm Action is circulating a citizen petition encouraging the FTC to investigate anticompetitive activity in the egg industry. Media Contact: Dee Laninga, [email protected], 202-450-0094 · Cal-Maine reported roughly $1.2 billion in profits during the egg price spike, yet this settlement lets dominant egg producers treat alleged price fixing as the cost of doing business rather than real accountability.|Update: See Farm Action’s February 2025 egg industry investigation and letter to the FTC here. January 19, 2023 — In response to record-high egg prices and just before testifying at an open meeting of the Federal Trade Commission (FTC), today Farm Action sent a letter urging the FTC “to promptly open an investigation into the egg industry, prosecute any violations of the antitrust laws it finds within, and ultimately, get the American people their money back.”|Farm Action’s letter lays out the economic basis for its “concerns over apparent price gouging, price coordination, and other unfair or deceptive acts or practices by dominant producers of eggs,” including market giant and industry “bellwether” Cal-Maine Foods.|“For the 26-week period ending on November 26, 2022, Cal-Maine reported a ten-fold year-over-year increase in gross profits — from $50.392 million to $535.339 million — and a five-fold increase in its gross margins,” the letter states.\"\nhash: ed57981616568b03\nembed_ref: farmaction.us-Wf3\napp_id: web\nskill_id: search",
