                "content": "app_id: web\nskill_id: search\nresult_count: 10\nembed_ids: 0f29384d-ab2d-4742-b17f-7f5ac12be2be|b4a7d9f1-f576-4205-9d30-2bd11d63d202|a2951fc9-cd42-4a42-adb9-c9064da604ea|83469c50-fedb-4833-9357-4c5fde8d467a|e9e6625d-14a2-49d9-ad81-509202d15983|b7aac3a6-6838-4b10-a945-69a4263bd17a|32be9413-0c4a-4b27-977a-e181d6a8fb9b|c76a5627-2862-425f-9350-102c8b946102|81cba532-cfb8-47be-91a6-41e60395b69a|255495e7-e5a5-4931-88bc-f54d1a42801f\nstatus: finished\nquery: USDA ERS egg production feed costs corn soybean meal 2022 2023 2024\nprovider: Brave Search\nid: 4\npreview_results[6]{title,url,meta_url_favicon,description}:\n  Poultry & Eggs | Economic Research Service - USDA,\"https://www.ers.usda.gov/topics/animal-products/poultry-eggs\",\"https://imgs.search.brave.com/sBVnG-cQD_Ec2W7sMNOQdp4UUIPn6Y02_dEeleMr1po/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMGU5YTMzN2Zm/OTU1YjhmNzg0Mjdj/NjEzOGNjNDZkYTBh/MTQ0NGFjN2I0ZDll/ZDk3NTc3OTQxZWQz/NmU0NDk4NS93d3cu/ZXJzLnVzZGEuZ292/Lw\",\"The associated database covers projections for the four major feed grains (corn, sorghum, barley, and oats), in addition to the other major feed crops and livestock. ERS also produces reports covering domestic and global conditions, trends, and policies that affect poultry supply, demand, prices, and trade in the egg and poultry sector.\"\n  Poultry & Eggs - Sector at a Glance | Economic Research Service,\"https://www.ers.usda.gov/topics/animal-products/poultry-eggs/sector-at-a-glance\",\"https://imgs.search.brave.com/sBVnG-cQD_Ec2W7sMNOQdp4UUIPn6Y02_dEeleMr1po/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMGU5YTMzN2Zm/OTU1YjhmNzg0Mjdj/NjEzOGNjNDZkYTBh/MTQ0NGFjN2I0ZDll/ZDk3NTc3OTQxZWQz/NmU0NDk4NS93d3cu/ZXJzLnVzZGEuZ292/Lw\",\"U.S. poultry production has a competitive global advantage due to abundant domestic feed resources, primarily soybean meal and corn. Feed is generally the most significant production cost across livestock, and poultry converts feed to human food products (meat and eggs) more efficiently than larger livestock.\"\n  Commodity Costs and Returns | Economic Research Service,\"https://www.ers.usda.gov/data-products/commodity-costs-and-returns\",\"https://imgs.search.brave.com/sBVnG-cQD_Ec2W7sMNOQdp4UUIPn6Y02_dEeleMr1po/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMGU5YTMzN2Zm/OTU1YjhmNzg0Mjdj/NjEzOGNjNDZkYTBh/MTQ0NGFjN2I0ZDll/ZDk3NTc3OTQxZWQz/NmU0NDk4NS93d3cu/ZXJzLnVzZGEuZ292/Lw\",\"USDA has estimated annual production costs and returns and published accounts for major field crop and livestock enterprises since 1975. Cost and return estimates are reported for the United States and major production regions for corn, soybeans, wheat, cotton, grain sorghum, rice, peanuts, oats, barley, milk, hogs, and cow-calf.\"\n  \"U.S. Egg Cost of Production and Prices January 9, 2024 Compiled by\",\"https://www.eggindustrycenter.org/media/cms/Costs_and_Prices_for_December_2023__36ED6C7DE3179.pdf\",\"https://imgs.search.brave.com/45bNO3gcAAwv5ZccJX5w96AdNQuYlq1T8SALvkTOqcY/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvNGMyM2FlYWZj/NjgyNDYwYTE1NDNh/ZmUwMDA4MzA1YjQ2/NWMxMWM5NmE0MWIz/ODc4MjE5ZmQzZmQ4/YjZmYjFiMy93d3cu/ZWdnaW5kdXN0cnlj/ZW50ZXIub3JnLw\",\"In December, corn prices were $72/ton (28%) lower than in the previous year. Soybean Meal prices were $12/ton ... The December 2023 egg value to producers was 269 cents/dozen (61%) lower than in December 2022.\"\n  \"Feed Grains Database - Feed Grains: Yearbook Tables | Economic Research Service\",\"https://www.ers.usda.gov/data-products/feed-grains-database/feed-grains-yearbook-tables\",\"https://imgs.search.brave.com/sBVnG-cQD_Ec2W7sMNOQdp4UUIPn6Y02_dEeleMr1po/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMGU5YTMzN2Zm/OTU1YjhmNzg0Mjdj/NjEzOGNjNDZkYTBh/MTQ0NGFjN2I0ZDll/ZDk3NTc3OTQxZWQz/NmU0NDk4NS93d3cu/ZXJzLnVzZGEuZ292/Lw\",\"This data product contains statistics on four feed grains (corn, grain sorghum, barley, and oats), foreign coarse grains (feed grains plus rye, millet, and mixed grains), hay, and related items. This includes data published in the monthly Feed Outlook and previously annual Feed Yearbook.\"\n  Feed Grains Database - Documentation | Economic Research Service,\"https://www.ers.usda.gov/data-products/feed-grains-database/documentation\",\"https://imgs.search.brave.com/sBVnG-cQD_Ec2W7sMNOQdp4UUIPn6Y02_dEeleMr1po/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMGU5YTMzN2Zm/OTU1YjhmNzg0Mjdj/NjEzOGNjNDZkYTBh/MTQ0NGFjN2I0ZDll/ZDk3NTc3OTQxZWQz/NmU0NDk4NS93d3cu/ZXJzLnVzZGEuZ292/Lw\",\"The major feed components of corn and soybeans account for 83–91 percent of the total ingredients in the rations. Data are presented in table 15. Monthly values are simple averages of daily prices reported by AMS. Annual values are simple averages of monthly prices for the marketing year, ...\"",
