                "content": "type: search_result\ntitle: Feed Cost Indices for Laying Hens in 2023 - Center for Commercial Agriculture\nurl: \"https://ag.purdue.edu/commercialag/home/resource/2022/11/feed-cost-indices-for-laying-hens-in-2023/\"\ndescription: Future prices for corn and soybean meal in early November were used to project feed cost indices through 2023. Figures 1 and 2 report monthly corn and soybean meal prices from January 2007 to September 2022.\nage: \"November 1, 2022\"\npage_age: \"November 1, 2022\"\nlanguage: en\nfamily_friendly: true\nprofile_name: Purdue College of Agriculture\nmeta_url_favicon: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/b37qUqIvf-hZ6tki0WRce8N9cCejJwdFJBAfkye-FMg/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvYzBjYTFkNTM0/MjQ1NmE2ZDM2ZWY0/OTNkMDE3ZmNlNzY4/MDZkNzBjYzZjNmUw/MjRiODFkOWZhOTdi/NTUxMDQwMC9hZy5w/dXJkdWUuZWR1Lw\"\nthumbnail_src: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/V2Lt2QY4McAPSOT-2xWmCwtRN5qXJbqH20A944s4ORQ/rs:fit:200:200:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cHM6Ly9hZy5w/dXJkdWUuZWR1L2Nv/bW1lcmNpYWxhZy9o/b21lL3dwLWNvbnRl/bnQvdXBsb2Fkcy8y/MDIyLzExLzIwMjIx/MTAxX0xhbmdlbWVp/ZXItRmVlZENvc3RJ/bmRpY2VzZm9yTGF5/aW5nSGVuc19GaWcx/LmpwZw\"\nthumbnail_original: \"https://ag.purdue.edu/commercialag/home/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/20221101_Langemeier-FeedCostIndicesforLayingHens_Fig1.jpg\"\nextra_snippets: \"Soybean meal and distillers’ grain prices were obtained from Feed Outlook, published monthly by USDA-ERS. Information from Agricultural Prices, a monthly USDA-NASS publication, was used to compute soybean oil and supplement prices. Future prices for corn and soybean meal in early November were used to project feed cost indices through 2023. Figures 1 and 2 report monthly corn and soybean meal prices from January 2007 to September 2022.|Soybean meal price averaged $357 per ton from 2007 to the current month. Recent corn and soybean meal prices are around $7.00 per bushel and $475 per ton, respectively. Though expected to drop in 2023, corn and soybean prices will remain substantially above the long-run averages. Figure 1. Monthly Indiana Corn Prices, 2007 to 2022|Annual feed cost indices for laying hens are presented in figure 4. The projections for 2022 and 2023 (red bars) used corn and soybean meal futures prices in early November. The projected feed cost index for 2023 is 116.3 which is 4.8 percent below the average index for 2022, but 16.3 percent above the index for 2021.|Current projections suggest that feed costs for 2023 will be slightly lower than those experienced in 2022. Feed costs are expected to be higher in the first one-half of the 2023 than the in the second half of 2023. Information related to feed costs for other livestock species can be found on the web site for the Center for Commercial Agriculture (purdue.edu/commercialag). ... USDA’s first 2026 Farm Income and Wealth Statistics release provides an early look at the U.S.\"\nhash: 03ad509cf6aa8a17\nembed_ref: ag.purdue.edu-zCS\napp_id: web\nskill_id: search",
