                "content": "type: search_result\ntitle: Feed Grains Database - Documentation | Economic Research Service\nurl: \"https://www.ers.usda.gov/data-products/feed-grains-database/documentation\"\ndescription: \"The major feed components of corn and soybeans account for 83–91 percent of the total ingredients in the rations. Data are presented in table 15. Monthly values are simple averages of daily prices reported by AMS. Annual values are simple averages of monthly prices for the marketing year, ...\"\nage: null\npage_age: null\nlanguage: en\nfamily_friendly: true\nprofile_name: Economic Research Service\nmeta_url_favicon: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/sBVnG-cQD_Ec2W7sMNOQdp4UUIPn6Y02_dEeleMr1po/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMGU5YTMzN2Zm/OTU1YjhmNzg0Mjdj/NjEzOGNjNDZkYTBh/MTQ0NGFjN2I0ZDll/ZDk3NTc3OTQxZWQz/NmU0NDk4NS93d3cu/ZXJzLnVzZGEuZ292/Lw\"\nthumbnail: null\nextra_snippets: \"This database contains statistics on four feed grains (corn, grain sorghum, barley, and oats), foreign coarse grains (feed grains plus rye, millet, and mixed grains), hay, animal unit indexes of grain and roughage, rail rate indexes, and grain shipments. This includes data published in the monthly Feed Outlook and the annual Feed Yearbook reports.|Annual values are simple averages of monthly prices for the marketing year calculated by ERS. Data are presented in tables 12–14. Annual values are simple averages of monthly ratios for the marketing year. National average prices are used in the calculation. Effective January 1995, prices of commercial feeds are based on current U.S. prices received for corn, soybeans, alfalfa hay, and all wheat.|The major feed components of corn and soybeans account for 83–91 percent of the total ingredients in the rations. Data are presented in table 15. Monthly values are simple averages of daily prices reported by AMS. Annual values are simple averages of monthly prices for the marketing year, calculated by ERS.|The data reported for high protein soybean meal prices reflect prices in Decatur, Illinois, before January 1999 and Central Illinois thereafter. Data are presented in table 16. Monthly values are simple averages of biweekly prices reported by Milling and Baking News, except for corn starch, which is calculated using proprietary data. Annual values are simple averages of monthly prices for the marketing year calculated by ERS.\"\nhash: cc0da5ee0b9d1e7f\nembed_ref: ers.usda.gov-yAY\napp_id: web\nskill_id: search",
