                "embed_id": "927489f9-3307-48ab-bcab-67a8d6b15ec6",
                "type": "website",
                "content": "type: search_result\ntitle: Egg Prices Crack $9 Mark Across California - LAmag\nurl: \"https://lamag.com/food/egg-prices-crack-9-mark-across-california/\"\ndescription: \"Some retailers have posted signs attributing shortages to California’s Proposition 12 cage-free requirements, but agricultural experts identify avian influenza as the primary market disruptor. Local restaurants feel the squeeze of these unprecedented costs. Some establishments search for better wholesale prices to shield customers from increases, while others have started raising menu prices on egg dishes to cope with the surge. The USDA’s latest data paints a sobering picture: nine confirmed avian flu cases across Merced, Stanislaus, Riverside, and San Joaquin counties last month alone.\"\nage: \"August 21, 2025\"\npage_age: \"August 21, 2025\"\nlanguage: en\nfamily_friendly: true\nprofile_name: LAmag\nmeta_url_favicon: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/cGG287tQDEBghWYEfCkfcIjGGc5R6nThbECP6MnjV98/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvODRkMDdhMzli/YzdkZTU0YjkxMTNk/NmFmYjUzMmI2OTlm/NWFiMDRhODRjNDdj/MzRiM2NlMmQxNDJj/Yjk4OTZhNi9sYW1h/Zy5jb20v\"\nthumbnail_src: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/OBuwjOAOVs9b1XKZSF7yr5sLerk-G3bNlvyPI_PEok4/rs:fit:200:200:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cHM6Ly9sYW1h/Zy5jb20vd3AtY29u/dGVudC91cGxvYWRz/LzIwMjUvMDEvY2Fs/aWZvcm5pYS1lZ2ct/cHJpY2VzLXNreXJv/Y2tldC10by04OTct/cGVyLWRvemVuLWFt/aWQtYmlyZC1mbHUt/Y3Jpc2lzLXNjYWxl/ZC5qcGc\"\nthumbnail_original: \"https://lamag.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/california-egg-prices-skyrocket-to-897-per-dozen-amid-bird-flu-crisis-scaled.jpg\"\nextra_snippets: \"Some retailers have posted signs attributing shortages to California’s Proposition 12 cage-free requirements, but agricultural experts identify avian influenza as the primary market disruptor. Local restaurants feel the squeeze of these unprecedented costs. Some establishments search for better wholesale prices to shield customers from increases, while others have started raising menu prices on egg dishes to cope with the surge. The USDA’s latest data paints a sobering picture: nine confirmed avian flu cases across Merced, Stanislaus, Riverside, and San Joaquin counties last month alone.|California egg prices surged nearly 60% in December due to a devastating bird flu outbreak and holiday demandCredit: Envato\"\nhash: 77bfe4e1fb153b70\nembed_ref: lamag.com-ENU\napp_id: web\nskill_id: search",
