                "content": "type: search_result\ntitle: \"California egg supplies limited by avian flu, cage-free rule - Valley Voice\"\nurl: \"https://www.ourvalleyvoice.com/2023/01/20/california-egg-supplies-limited-by-avian-flu-cage-free-rule/\"\ndescription: \"Proposition 2, which passed in 2008, mandated more room for hens to extend their wings, stand up, lie down and turn around. Proposition 12, which voters approved in 2018, phased out caged housing systems altogether.\"\nage: \"January 20, 2023\"\npage_age: \"January 20, 2023\"\nlanguage: en\nfamily_friendly: true\nprofile_name: Valley Voice\nmeta_url_favicon: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/OMuwpzKE68Fgu3EWW2B6IHG-IJRgnBvfqdq7kjah-0k/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvYzkwNjFkOTVh/MDFlNjMzNjk5NDE1/NjVmNTMzOWU0ODQx/NjA1ZjEyNTNiZDQ5/Y2ExNGI4MTMxNGNl/ZDRkNjFkZC93d3cu/b3VydmFsbGV5dm9p/Y2UuY29tLw\"\nthumbnail_src: \"https://imgs.search.brave.com/Y1y2nowFgqgXOD6aBtXNj7-6K8rLmN7MUDfxOil2kig/rs:fit:200:200:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cu/b3VydmFsbGV5dm9p/Y2UuY29tL3dwLWNv/bnRlbnQvdXBsb2Fk/cy8yMDE4LzAxL3Z2/LWdvb2dsZS5wbmc\"\nthumbnail_original: \"https://www.ourvalleyvoice.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/vv-google.png\"\nextra_snippets: \"Even with eggs in short supply nationwide and prices climbing to new heights, it has not been enough to keep a 100-year-old egg farm from going out of business. John Lewis Jr., president of Farmer John Egg Farm in Bakersfield, confirmed that the family operation will close its doors by the end of the month.|At 75, Lewis has been in the egg business for 50 years and would “still rather be a farmer…rather be out there in the chicken coop.” The farm once maintained 300,000 egg layers but stopped production last year when Proposition 12, the cage-free mandate, went into effect.|Proposition 2, which passed in 2008, mandated more room for hens to extend their wings, stand up, lie down and turn around. Proposition 12, which voters approved in 2018, phased out caged housing systems altogether.|Proposition 12 also requires producers from other states to not use cages if they want to sell their eggs in California.\"\nhash: fac4b6d5a188e29e\nembed_ref: ourvalleyvoice.com-gzV\napp_id: web\nskill_id: search",
